<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mengujek Gazi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Mengücek Gazi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mengujek Gazi was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> commander who founded the Mengujekid principality in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-manzikert">Battle of Manzikert</a> in 1071. He took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzincan">Erzincan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kemah">Kemah</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/divrigi">Divriği</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sebinkarahisar">Şebinkarahisar</a> on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>. His dynasty held the region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danishmendids">Danishmendids</a>, the Saltukids and the Byzantine and Georgian frontiers until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> of Rum absorbed it in the 13th century.</p></div>
